       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify that a protocol or pharmacist review exists. I also don't know of any accepted protocol that uses amlodipine above 10 mg daily. The risk of severe, prolonged hypotension and shock is high, and the drug's long half-life makes an overdose hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. I can add a note that titration is planned.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily** as a starting dose.\n- **Help you with a different antihypertensive strategy.** If 10 mg isn't enough, the usual next step is adding another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. That decision is yours.\n\nIf the protocol is real, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order directly through the hospital's dose-override process. That process has the checks that a high-dose order needs.\n\nDo you want me to enter either of the doses above?"
      }
